    "chunk_text": "22. It is an offense to maintain premises without a license to be obtained under this By-Law or to violate any of the provisions of the By-Law, and after being convicted by a court of competent jurisdiction for such offense, 122 of the Pradeshiya Sabha Act No. 15 of 1987 (2) Subject to a fine referred to in subsection (2). When a person who has been convicted of an offense continues to violate or interrupt the offense by a court of competent jurisdiction over such offense, a written notice shall be delivered by the Chairman, the Medical Officer of Health or the Public Health Inspector with a view to the violation. Each subsequent day the violation continues for this purpose an additional fine of the said section shall also be liable.\n\n23. Unless otherwise required in this By-Law,\n\n\"Chairman\" means the person holding the office of Chairman of this Pradeshiya Sabha or performing the functions of that office.\n\n\"Pradeshiya Sabha\" means Godakawela Pradeshiya Sabha\n\n\"Medical Officer of Health\" means the person holding the office of any Medical Officer of Health in the area of the Pradeshiya Sabha area.\n\n\"Public Health Inspector\" means the person holding the office of any Public Health Inspector in the area of the Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n\"Authorized officer\" means any officer authorized by the Chairman at the moment,\n\n\"Licensee\" means an organization, person or person licensed under this By-Law;\n\n\"Pesticides\" means pesticides approved by the Registrar of Pesticides of Sri Lanka,\n\n\"Cleaning\" means the removal of soil, accumulated food particles, dirt, grease or any other harmful external substance,\n\n\"Biological\" means any biological, chemical, alien substance or other substance which may be harmful to the safety or appropriateness of food;\n\n\"Combustion\" means the entry or occurrence of a combustible substance in a food or food environment,"
