    "md5": "2c4d7dbafb70461e1f26672cc48ef0ae",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2037,
    "chunk_text": "THIS is to notify that I, Dhamma Dissanayake, Governor of the Sabaragamuwa Province has approved the By-law regarding Prevention of Public Disturbances in the Distribution of Free Food within authoritative area of Balangoda Pradeshiya Sabha, prepared by the Balangoda Pradeshiya Sabha by virtue of powers vested in it under Section 122 read with Section 126 of Pradeshiya Sabha Act, No. 15 of 1987 and passed at its General meeting held on 20.06.2019, by\n\n54 A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.12.05 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.12.2019\n\nBy-Law on the Prevention of Public Disturbances in the Distribution of Free Food within Balangoda\n\nPradeshiya Sabha Authoritative Area\n\n1. This by-law is enacted to protect the health of the public and the associated public health in the authoritative area of the Balangoda Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n2. This by-law is known as the by-law for the Prevention of Public Persecution in the Distribution of Free Food in the Balangoda Pradeshiya Sabha Authoritative Area.\n\n3. If any person, society or organization in the area of authority of the Pradeshiya Sabha intends to produce or distribute food for free distribution or supply or for any other special purpose for this purpose an application under the form specified in the first schedule of this by-law should be submitted to the Balangoda Pradeshiya Sabha (Hereafter known as the Pradeshiya Sabha) and obtain a license.\n\n4. The Chairman shall not issue the relevant permit unless the following conditions have been fulfilled in granting the permit.\n\n4.(1) No person shall maintain a place where food is served or distributed free of charge for any promotional purpose within the area of authority of the Pradeshiya Sabha, unless there is a permit obtained from the mayor of the Pradeshiya Sabha on the report of the relevant public health inspector and the Medical Officer."
  },
